{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/865675-retroactive-cover","id":865675,"title":"Retroactive Cover?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-14T13:39:25-07:00","id":865675,"title":"Retroactive Cover?","content":"So. In the World of Darkness(Or Chronicles. Or Whatever.) there are some creatures that tend to live painfully long lives, take for example Mummies and Vampires. And we know for a fact that Demons can make Pacts with those beings.<br /> So what would happen if a Demon bought from a, let's say, Elder Vampire for a bit of said Elder's life that took part back in, let's say, XVth century? Can a Demon even bargain for such a piece of identity? Would it be possible to craft a patchwork Cover from those bits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T13:51:10-07:00","id":865686,"title":"","content":"Possible, sure. A good idea, not so much. At best you could construct a patchwork cover that is of that supernatural type, but then you have the same problem as Soul Pacting a modern vampire only worse, you'd look like one, but wouldn't have the memories, or abilities to back it up.<br /> <br /> And just patching a piece of that in would be hell on any modern cover.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T16:25:06-07:00","id":865743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/865675-retroactive-cover?p=865686#post865686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Possible, sure. A good idea, not so much. At best you could construct a patchwork cover that is of that supernatural type, but then you have the same problem as Soul Pacting a modern vampire only worse, you'd look like one, but wouldn't have the memories, or abilities to back it up.<br /> <br /> And just patching a piece of that in would be hell on any modern cover.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see it having use in a time travelling campaign.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T16:28:55-07:00","id":865747,"title":"","content":"Show of power and deep cover could have you covered for maintaining the illusion if you did try to pass yourself off as a vampire.<br /> <br /> The real question is if you used show of power to mimic a vampires feeding would you convert it to vitae? (What if you learnt how to convert to aether instead even if a gadget was required)<br /> <br /> Edit: on the topic of your initial question since both parties are still alive you should be able to take any part of what you could normally take from a mortal. The one thing to caution is there would likely be compromise if your cover's father has been dead for centuries unless you are acting as a vampire and even then if a mortal learnt it could still potentially cause comprises.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2909,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","user":"Mr.F.I.X.","date":". 04-14-2016, 07:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T07:03:42-07:00","id":865925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/865675-retroactive-cover?p=865747#post865747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The real question is if you used show of power to mimic a vampires feeding would you convert it to vitae? (What if you learnt how to convert to aether instead even if a gadget was required)</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see an implanted Near-Field Raw Materials gadget that could do that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T08:11:52-07:00","id":865951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/865675-retroactive-cover?p=865925#post865925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see an implanted Near-Field Raw Materials gadget that could do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lambda with Show of Power and Raw Materials?<br /> <br /> I mean, while the character is merely using it to better imitate a vampire, being able to extract Aether from mere human blood is a powerful advantage to the Unchained.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T11:58:45-07:00","id":866034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/865675-retroactive-cover?p=865951#post865951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lambda with Show of Power and Raw Materials?<br /> <br /> I mean, while the character is merely using it to better imitate a vampire, being able to extract Aether from mere human blood is a powerful advantage to the Unchained.</div> </div> </div> </div>By it being a lambda it makes sense both thematically and mechanically. It should be rarer than just an exploited gadget as well as more difficult / risky to make, I agree. Raw materials could be an interesting choice as malonkey1 suggested. Though the main reason a NFE of show of power would be better in my opinion is because it'd be subverting the conversion of blood to vitae (the mimiced ability) to another energy form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T12:26:05-07:00","id":866052,"title":"","content":"To be honest, &quot;just&quot; a Show of Power Gadget with the ability to turn consumed blood to Vitae would be something a lot of Ghouls would <i>kill</i> for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T13:07:50-07:00","id":866071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/865675-retroactive-cover?p=866052#post866052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, &quot;just&quot; a Show of Power Gadget with the ability to turn consumed blood to Vitae would be something a lot of Ghouls would <i>kill</i> for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heck, what about a modified Gadget (Show of Power, or the Show of Power + Raw Materials Lambda) that turned electricity into Vitae? (Mimic the Promethean Transmutation to generate Pyros from electricity, modified to convert it into Vitae instead). I'm <i>sure</i> a Demon would be willing to sell you one - just sign here.<br /> <br /> ...And the resulting war over the ownership of said item is an instant plot hook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T15:57:39-07:00","id":866153,"title":"","content":"Well at least that explains how you'd convince a vampire to sell off such crucial details that ground their humanity. Self sufficient ghouls (potentially self feeding) that can gather their own vitae and also bring it back to their master. For the aether to maintain such 'fangs' the demon could definitely gain a powerful ally.<br /> <br /> On the original topic of pacts for 'impossible details' though, what if you bought the relationship a vampire has with their Sire? Of course it would not give you the ability to appear like a vampire (show of power or deep cover for that) but it could provide you with an in to gain a potentially great ally or shrouded place to hide from the machine.<br /> <br /> Tangental thought but what effect could vitae have on a demon while in cover? Yes, you have to worry about addition to vitae or the blood bond but I mean something far grander. Could the life of a cover be extended beyond a mortal life span by being ghouled? Oh it would be a foolish thing and you'd have to reinvent yourself every few decades (as a vampire does) but what if a demon could live out their potential immortality with a single face? If this wouldn't be supported by the standard mechanisms of cover could the embed going native, though use or tailored gadget allow it? [ My current demon is a mad scientist so I have to think outside the box ]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T10:38:32-07:00","id":866439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/865675-retroactive-cover?p=866153#post866153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tangental thought but what effect could vitae have on a demon while in cover? Yes, you have to worry about addition to vitae or the blood bond but I mean something far grander. Could the life of a cover be extended beyond a mortal life span by being ghouled? Oh it would be a foolish thing and you'd have to reinvent yourself every few decades (as a vampire does) but what if a demon could live out their potential immortality with a single face? If this wouldn't be supported by the standard mechanisms of cover could the embed going native, though use or tailored gadget allow it? [ My current demon is a mad scientist so I have to think outside the box ]</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I've got one Demon character that essentially rebuilds one of their Patch Job Covers every so often. They trade around dots and cover elements until there is nothing left, then recreate the Patch Job (plus or minus a few details, to reflect the changing times) at the desired age. Complicated and time consuming, but it works.<br /> <br /> Another option, if you are willing to bend details or use some homebrew, is to just give the Cover life extending Supernatural Merits, such as <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=847701#post847701\">Supernatural Integration</a>, and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/786694-homebrew-demon-merits?p=848953#post848953\">Longevity/Ageless</a> (or Psychic Vampire from Hurt Locker).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T16:27:03-07:00","id":866562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/865675-retroactive-cover?p=866439#post866439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, I've got one Demon character that essentially rebuilds one of their Patch Job Covers every so often. They trade around dots and cover elements until there is nothing left, then recreate the Patch Job (plus or minus a few details, to reflect the changing times) at the desired age. Complicated and time consuming, but it works.</div> </div> </div> </div>How does it work, actually?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T18:58:13-07:00","id":866599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Inquisitor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/865675-retroactive-cover?p=866562#post866562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does it work, actually?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Mr. Green creates a number of transfer Pacts, moving Cover elements that he desires to keep off the Cover (which reduces its Cover rating). Usually to himself, though occassionally to another trusted Demon temporarily if he can't afford the abysmal Willpower costs at the moment. Once the Cover is dissolved, he creates a &quot;new&quot; Patch Job Cover with the same name, incorporating pretty much all of the old elements (plus or minus a few). Voila - meet the new Cover, same as the old Cover, but set at a different starting age (since nothing really says you can't decide on such details, provided they aren't relevant to Cover elements). It's a lot of trouble, but he's attached to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T08:50:37-07:00","id":867592,"title":"","content":"Somewhat off topic, though still rather on point while talking about Soul Pacts and Pacts in general, also something I've come to realize that many people either gloss over, or it just never has come up: Why doesn't anyone include memories to the Soul Pact ( I'm leaving the whole business and drawbacks with the supernatural and soul pacts out for a moment, but I'll get back to it.. maybe). While Pacting away experiences and aspects of one's identity is part and parcel for Pacts.. no one ever seems to address the impact memories have. What one has experienced, and how they perceive and more importantly remember are big parts of one's identity.. and it just never made sense to me as to why memories were never included. This glaring absence the one thing that makes Soul Pacts more or less useless in my opinion, and makes them, at least to me on how the rules for Cover work, virtually untenable- because no matter how long one observes, even the demon's perfect memory and ample time to study.. it is impossible to stay in Cover with a Soul Pact.. at least for anything longer than a few months or a year ( if lucky) now depending one what you have to do and if you are using the Soul Pact simply to gain advantages other Pacts cant offer, that's fine.. I just find them incredibly not worth it, for how little you truly get.<br /> <br /> I don't know, I just think that when it comes to completely overtaking a humans existence for yourself.. you should at least also possess the memories. It makes acting in Cover easier and to reference Fallen, it would of been a nice overlap with how the possession of a human host worked. ( though not having the Translation guide, I'm prolly talking out my ass cause this is addressed and such a thing is an option xD) Then again, I do see cover as much more than just a suit of flesh and blood.<br /> <br /> anyway, bitching over. Now how this could work for retroactively placing aspects of an ancient being into a pact, their memories ( however hazy) would be a great source of information.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 04-18-2016, 12:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T10:47:51-07:00","id":867661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/865675-retroactive-cover?p=867592#post867592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Somewhat off topic, though still rather on point while talking about Soul Pacts and Pacts in general, also something I've come to realize that many people either gloss over, or it just never has come up: Why doesn't anyone include memories to the Soul Pact ( I'm leaving the whole business and drawbacks with the supernatural and soul pacts out for a moment, but I'll get back to it.. maybe). While Pacting away experiences and aspects of one's identity is part and parcel for Pacts.. no one ever seems to address the impact memories have. What one has experienced, and how they perceive and more importantly remember are big parts of one's identity.. and it just never made sense to me as to why memories were never included. This glaring absence the one thing that makes Soul Pacts more or less useless in my opinion, and makes them, at least to me on how the rules for Cover work, virtually untenable- because no matter how long one observes, even the demon's perfect memory and ample time to study.. it is impossible to stay in Cover with a Soul Pact.. at least for anything longer than a few months or a year ( if lucky) now depending one what you have to do and if you are using the Soul Pact simply to gain advantages other Pacts cant offer, that's fine.. I just find them incredibly not worth it, for how little you truly get.<br /> <br /> I don't know, I just think that when it comes to completely overtaking a humans existence for yourself.. you should at least also possess the memories. It makes acting in Cover easier and to reference Fallen, it would of been a nice overlap with how the possession of a human host worked. ( though not having the Translation guide, I'm prolly talking out my ass cause this is addressed and such a thing is an option xD) Then again, I do see cover as much more than just a suit of flesh and blood.<br /> <br /> anyway, bitching over. Now how this could work for retroactively placing aspects of an ancient being into a pact, their memories ( however hazy) would be a great source of information.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not possessing the memories is a key part of risk, but, honestly, it's not much of one in most cases. Most people don't expect other people to get replaced by body-snatchers or for you to perfectly recall every shared moment or experience in life. Demons are expected to be able to lie or bluff their way past much of it, and research the major details.<br /> <br /> In short, possessing the memories isn't that much of a limitation, but simply being there offers story hooks that getting all the memories would shut down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T12:41:29-07:00","id":867743,"title":"","content":"I don't know. Sure it offers story hooks, but it doesn't offer the story hooks that I want to explore. The core book actually offers an example of the kind of complications possessing a humans memories alongside ones own and how that can heavily affect an angel or demon in unexpected and pretty powerful ways. To me that is more compelling than simply faking it and living the lie as a permanent actor with only observations and research to go on- and make Compromise rolls a but more interesting, seeing as that conflict of identity would be more tangible and less of a mechanical abstraction- as it feels to be for me ( Soul Pacts are easily the most &quot;Game-y&quot; options for Cover and feel too artificial, though not in a good, Immersive way for me.) In short, I feel that having memories be an alternative option would add a depth to a Soul Pact that it lacks, as opposed to normal pact methods. But hey that's just me and every body is free to play how they wanna play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 04-18-2016, 03:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T13:09:37-07:00","id":867762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/865675-retroactive-cover?p=867743#post867743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know. Sure it offers story hooks, but it doesn't offer the story hooks that I want to explore. The core book actually offers an example of the kind of complications possessing a humans memories alongside ones own and how that can heavily affect an angel or demon in unexpected and pretty powerful ways. To me that is more compelling than simply faking it and living the lie as a permanent actor with only observations and research to go on- and make Compromise rolls a but more interesting, seeing as that conflict of identity would be more tangible and less of a mechanical abstraction- as it feels to be for me ( Soul Pacts are easily the most &quot;Game-y&quot; options for Cover and feel too artificial, though not in a good, Immersive way for me.) In short, I feel that having memories be an alternative option would add a depth to a Soul Pact that it lacks, as opposed to normal pact methods. But hey that's just me and every body is free to play how they wanna play.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, there are methods of mind reading and memory downloading. Use those.<br /> <br /> Or narrate the personality synthesis as a glitch in the normal Soul Pact process. With a little as Demon's truly understand about their own nature and mechanisms, and all the other weirdness encountered, its not that hard of a sell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T13:24:55-07:00","id":867775,"title":"","content":"Sure, but I like the idea of being able to just include memories in the particulars of the Pact, since memories can be bought and traded in the world of darkness, surely Pacts can do the same","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T13:48:23-07:00","id":867800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/865675-retroactive-cover?p=867743#post867743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know. Sure it offers story hooks, but it doesn't offer the story hooks that I want to explore. The core book actually offers an example of the kind of complications possessing a humans memories alongside ones own and how that can heavily affect an angel or demon in unexpected and pretty powerful ways. To me that is more compelling than simply faking it and living the lie as a permanent actor with only observations and research to go on- and make Compromise rolls a but more interesting, seeing as that conflict of identity would be more tangible and less of a mechanical abstraction- as it feels to be for me ( Soul Pacts are easily the most &quot;Game-y&quot; options for Cover and feel too artificial, though not in a good, Immersive way for me.) In short, I feel that having memories be an alternative option would add a depth to a Soul Pact that it lacks, as opposed to normal pact methods. But hey that's just me and every body is free to play how they wanna play.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree. i always played it as when a Cover degraded, the demon would begin to forget parts of the cover's life, like Ms. Book in the opening fiction. It's been quite fun actually, because it makes for a great sense of disconnection and loss. It usually ends up being the relatively minor things that the Demon forgets, like where they went on their last birthday or something, but you actually get the feeling that it's not just a disguise, it's a life, falling to pieces around you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T14:08:47-07:00","id":867806,"title":"","content":"Same here, I play the Cover as something that is to be invested in not just because it keeps the angels off your tail, but because that despite there being a quantum disconnection; Every Cover is still a part of you- the baggage should be emotional and mental too rather than just outside sources from the connections to that Cover. That's a big reason why Soul Pacts are so &quot;Bleh&quot; to me, you step into them; but you lack those connections the person had to ground them; so you have to fumble, yes fumble despite what people say how perfect recall makes such things easy ( though it doesn't actually.. least it largely doesnt. perfect recall doesn't impart skill, a bad actor is still a bad actor, if he doesn't have the experience(s) to aid him- no matter how well remembered the script is. Legend helps though.. sort of. ) while you focus on puting on a good performance. Now some people can make this work well, as most role players should. . But I still don't like how Soul Pacts are nothing more than living suits rather than the full identities they are supposed to be. But I think I've detracted too much from the main topic now. <br /> <br /> Reading over everything, my answer is sadly more of the same; perfectly possible but the drawbacks make it difficult to use without really clever wording and structure of the Pact + use of other supernatural abilities to govern it. Now that I think of it, Legend could actually be fairly invaluable. Not for overtly supernatural things, but if the Cover is expected to know and indeed did possess lots of knowledge, yeah Legend is a good way to periodically make use of it in a limited fashion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 04-18-2016, 05:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}